  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=2x^4+x^2+ax+b$. When $P(x)$ is divided by $x+1$, the remainder is $4$. When $P(x)$ is divided by $x-2$, the remainder is $1$. Find $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p14-q25-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=-12,\\quad b=-11",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q25-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P(-1)=4",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P(2)=1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", then solve simultaneously.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "By the remainder theorem, $P(-1)=4$ and $P(2)=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(-1)^4+(-1)^2+a(-1)+b&=4\\\\3-a+b&=4\\\\-a+b&=1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2(2)^4+(2)^2+2a+b&=1\\\\36+2a+b&=1\\\\2a+b&=-35\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract the first coefficient equation from the second.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2a+b)-(-a+b)&=-35-1\\\\3a&=-36\\\\a&=-12\\\\b&=1+a\\\\b&=-11\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
